{"repo": {"timestamp": 1788651303000}, "packages": {"com.freedomfighter.baristatimer": {"versions": {"4f4933d57384be9a668f18ebb3fccb034f0387cc8ae8c75dea865130fa189d7c": null}}, "com.freedomfighter.readerslauncher": {"metadata": {"lastUpdated": 1788650946000, "description": {"en-US": "Reader's Launcher turns the home screen into a single column of words. No icons,\nno colours, no wallpaper: white on black, or black on white — flip between the two\nwith a double tap, from the \"Reader's theme\" quick-settings tile, or in settings.\n\n* Tiles are plain text: an app, or a category that opens a text list of apps.\n* A grid of 3 to 5 squares pinned at the bottom holds the unavoidable apps (phone,\n  messages…) with their icons rendered as monochrome glyphs.\n* Built-in widgets: clock; weather (Open-Meteo, no account, tap for five days);\n  agenda (next event, swipe for the following ones); tasks (first task of a\n  Tasks.org list, tick to complete, + to add — Tasks.org syncs with CalDAV, Google\n  Tasks, Microsoft To Do or keeps lists offline). Standard app widgets can be added too.\n* Swipe up for the alphabetical app list with search and the usual long-press\n  actions (add to home, category, rename, hide, app info, uninstall).\n* Swipe up and hold on the home screen for a text list of recently used apps.\n* Swipe down for notifications. Export and import the whole setup as a JSON file.\n* Two books beside the home screen: swipe right or left to read (EPUB, MOBI, FB2,\n  text), tap to turn pages, position remembered per book. Reading made effortless.\n* English by default; French, German, Spanish, Portuguese and Russian when the device\n  uses them.\n\nSerif, sans or monospace; three text sizes; left or centred. No ads, no tracking.\n"}}, "versions": {"b8f699ac66b407eda9f20a4d7e54f106b335b97052c590843fcf5ddaea278e28": null, "ac392fb6ed38c4d10a959db56e630fe011cfbbff68b75201162e41629dcfbb79": {"added": 1788650946000, "file": {"name": "/ReadersLauncher-v1.2.1.apk", "sha256